functions.plate:
Host 0x25 sdPstmSetVol. r0 = cmd[2] = port | 0x20 (ch0) | 0x10 (ch1); r1/r2 ch0 vol/fade, r4/r5 ch1 vol/fade.
r12 = g_pstm_player[port*2]. Body 0x6E30 per selected channel (flags|=CHG_VOL, fade step/interval via pcm_fade_calc);
pcm_next_ch (0x6E64) moves to ch1 or returns from this routine.

Host 0x11 sdShotPlay (handler 0x51F4 validated SOSB magic/version/ENDB). r0 port, r1 data number, r2 prio<<3, r3 SOSB.
num > count -> err 4 (QUIRK: num == count accepted). pcm_slot_alloc(kind 1); copy the SOSP register image
(SA + bank address, 16 regs 0x08-0x44); latch disdl_base/isel/imxl/pcms/pan_base/tl_base, pitch_base = PITCH read back;
pcm_apply_params; loops_default = SOSP+0x28, shot_loops_apply(loop_mode, ring_len); clear PAUSE, LFORE;
dummy MON_EG/MON_CA reads; key on (0x81D8).
QUIRKs: SA_LO = 0x8000 transient write; pcms taken from SA_LO bits 8:7.

Write a player's mix state to its channel. loop_count = 0; TL = clamp(tl + 0x100 - 2*volume) -> byte 0x29 + pl->tl;
DIPAN = pan_lin_to_aica_b[clamp(pan_aica_to_lin_b[pan_base] + pan/4 - 0x20, 0, 31)] -> byte 0x24 + pl->dipan;
pcm_apply_pitch(r4); DISDL = pcm_level_mix(direct_lvl, disdl_base); ISEL = fx_ch (bit6) or isel;
IMXL via the FxLev tail at 0x7038. Clears CHG_VOL/CHG_PAN if no fade interval.
